<main id="main"><div class="container"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="index.html">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page"><span>Non-Warrantable Condo Loans in Miami</span></li></ol></nav></div><section class="hero"><div class="container hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Alternative condo financing</p><h1>Non-Warrantable Condo Loans in Miami</h1><p>Financing options for Miami condo buildings that may not fit standard agency warrantability rules.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Review My Condo Building</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="mortgage-calculator-florida.html">Start Review</a></div><div class="trust-row"><span class="trust-pill">Matthew Gromadzki</span><span class="trust-pill">NMLS #2560919</span><span class="trust-pill">Miami · Florida</span><span class="trust-pill">Call (305) 988-4806</span></div></div><div class="hero-panel rate-card"><div class="rate-item"><span>Best first step</span><strong>Preapproval</strong></div><div class="rate-item"><span>Core review</span><strong>Payment + cash to close</strong></div><div class="rate-item"><span>Miami focus</span><strong>Condo + jumbo checks</strong></div><a class="btn btn-primary full" href="start.html">Send Scenario</a></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container two-col"><article class="prose"><p>Some Miami condo buildings do not fit standard agency guidelines. That does not always mean financing is impossible, but it may require a different lender, different down payment, different pricing, or a portfolio-style loan option.</p><p>Non-warrantable factors can include litigation, investor concentration, reserves, insurance issues, hotel/condo structure, short-term rentals, commercial space, or association financial concerns.</p><h2>Common non-warrantable issues</h2><p>A building may be considered non-warrantable when it does not meet standard condo project guidelines. Miami buyers often run into this with high-rise buildings, waterfront properties, buildings with pending repairs, or properties with flexible rental policies.</p><p>The best path is to review the building early before appraisal and underwriting deadlines become urgent.</p><h2>How alternative condo financing works</h2><p>Alternative condo loans may look at borrower strength, down payment, reserves, building risk, and loan amount differently from agency loans. Pricing and terms may be different, so it is important to compare the full monthly payment and cash to close.</p><p>A mortgage broker can help compare available lender options instead of relying on one bank’s condo overlay.</p></article><aside><form class="lead-form lead-form-compact" method="post" action="quote.html" data-lead-form><h2>Request a Non-Warrantable Condo Loans Miami Quote</h2><p>Answer a few basics and we’ll review the best mortgage path for your scenario.</p><input type="hidden" name="source_page" value="preview"><label>Loan goal<select name="loan_goal" required><option value="">Select one</option><option>Buying a home</option><option>Refinancing</option><option>Cash-out refinance</option><option>Investment property</option><option>Condo financing</option></select></label><div class="form-row"><label>Purchase price / value<input name="property_value" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="$650,000"></label><label>Down payment / equity<input name="down_payment" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="$100,000"></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Credit score range<select name="credit_score"><option value="">Select range</option><option>760+</option><option>720–759</option><option>680–719</option><option>640–679</option><option>Below 640</option><option>Not sure</option></select></label><label>Property city<input name="property_city" placeholder="Miami"></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Name<input name="name" autocomplete="name" required></label><label>Phone<input name="phone" autocomplete="tel" required></label></div><label>Email<input name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required></label><button class="btn btn-primary full" type="submit">Start Mortgage Review</button><p class="form-note">No obligation. Mortgage options depend on underwriting, lender guidelines, property type, and documentation.</p></form></aside></div></section><section class="section soft"><div class="container"><div class="cta-band"><div><p class="eyebrow">Fast next step</p><h2>Get a mortgage scenario review before you make a decision.</h2><p>Send purchase price, down payment, credit range, income type, and property city. The goal is to compare real options, not guess based on generic rates.</p></div><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Start Review</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="tel:+13059884806">Call (305) 988-4806</a></div></div></div></section><section class="section faq-section"><div class="container narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h2>Non-Warrantable Condo Loans in Miami FAQ</h2><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Can a non-warrantable condo still be financed?</summary><p>Often yes, but it may require a specialized lender or portfolio loan option. Approval depends on the borrower, the building, and the specific issue.</p></details><details><summary>Do non-warrantable condo loans cost more?</summary><p>They may have different pricing, down payment, and reserve requirements. A full quote is needed to compare the cost against other options.</p></details><details><summary>When should I check condo eligibility?</summary><p>Before making an offer whenever possible, especially in buildings with litigation, assessments, flexible rentals, or unusual ownership structures.</p></details></div></div></section><section class="section related-section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Keep comparing</p><h2>Related mortgage pages</h2><div class="card-grid small-grid"><a class="mini-card" href="condo-loans-miami.html">Condo Loans Miami<span>→</span></a>